{
  "surface": "gcp/security-command-center-findings-bigquery",
  "provider": "gcp",
  "reference": {
    "title": "Stream findings to BigQuery for analysis (dataset structure: findings table) + REST Resource: organizations.sources.findings (Finding object)",
    "url": "https://cloud.google.com/security-command-center/docs/how-to-analyze-findings-in-big-query",
    "consulted_at": "2026-10-14"
  },
  "delivery": {
    "kind": "bigquery",
    "path_template": "projects/{PROJECT_ID}/datasets/{DATASET_ID}/findings",
    "format": "bigquery-native-table",
    "compression": "not-applicable"
  },
  "reference_urls": {
    "continuous_export": "https://cloud.google.com/security-command-center/docs/how-to-analyze-findings-in-big-query",
    "bulk_export": "https://cloud.google.com/security-command-center/docs/bulk-exports-to-big-query",
    "finding_object_v1": "https://docs.cloud.google.com/security-command-center/docs/reference/rest/v1/organizations.sources.findings",
    "finding_discovery_v1": "https://securitycenter.googleapis.com/$discovery/rest?version=v1",
    "finding_object_v2": "https://cloud.google.com/security-command-center/docs/reference/rest/v2/organizations.sources.findings"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Both export mechanisms exist and are officially documented: continuous (streaming, recommended) and bulk (on-demand snapshot). Both write to a BigQuery table named 'findings', clustered by source_id, finding_id, event_time.",
    "The export pages document only 6 top-level columns and their descriptions. They do NOT declare BigQuery types, so 'type' is left null for those columns and the item is listed in 'unverified'.",
    "The export pages state that nested fields of the 'finding' column are the API reference 'Finding' object. The 68 top-level Finding fields below are transcribed verbatim from the v1 REST resource page.",
    "The export pages point to an API reference 'Resource' object for the 'resource' column, but no such SCC REST page is reachable (v1/Resource, v1/Asset, v1/organizations.assets all returned HTTP 404 on 2026-10-14). Its fields are therefore unverified.",
    "Nested sub-objects of Finding (indicator.*, vulnerability.*, access.*, compliance.*, ...) exist per the v1 page but their inner fields were not transcribed in this pass and are listed in 'unverified'.",
    "The documented event_time example is '2019-09-26 12:48:00.985000 UTC' (not RFC 3339 in the document's own example).",
    "The four Finding enums (State, Severity, Mute, FindingClass) were read in the machine contract finding_discovery_v1 -- the Security Center v1 discovery -- because the HTML reference page is 1.1 MB and the reader truncates exactly the sections carrying the constants. The COLUMNS cite the documentation page (finding_object_v1), not the discovery: is_official_url() accepts the documentation host and rejects the googleapis endpoint, and that division is the right one -- a column cites documentation, and the machine contract is the reading that proved the documentation had not been read carefully enough. Both agree; the discovery is what proved the FindingClass list ends at SECRET."
  ],
